  },
  "verdict": {
    "headline": "Network-Tg is the highest-value UNVALIDATED coating-science gap. The in-tree ML (MAE 39.1 C, r~0.08) and raw Van Krevelen (MAE 109.1 C) both FAIL because they use linear-polymer physics on a crosslinked network. The correct physics -- exact non-circular crosslink density (from the verified EEW/AHEW core) + ring/rotatable rigidity -- is prototyped here and shows real signal (ring-fraction Pearson r=+0.69, n=10; LOO MAE ~24-29 C direction-only, ring-only 24 C / +crosslink 29 C). It is NOT yet a Phase-0 KPI: rights-clean cited Tg is n=5 single-source with +/-20-30 C inter-lab scatter. One rights-clean cited dataset (>=12 systems, controlled cure) converts this into a defensible KPI.",
    "phase": "PRE_PHASE_0",
    "status": "CORRECT_PHYSICS_IDENTIFIED__BLOCKED_ON_RIGHTS_CLEAN_DATA"
  }
